<%# The Mind graph (mind graph canvas spec §3.2, §5): a frame. The graph's data
    is NOT in the page -- at the cap it is several hundred kilobytes, which
    would sit in every load and in Turbo's page cache -- so `admin--mind-graph`
    fetches it from `data-url`, lays it out in a worker (`data-worker-url`,
    which imports d3-force from `data-d3-url`: an import map does not apply
    inside a worker, so both are plain asset URLs) and draws it on the canvas.
    The canvas is one image to assistive technology; what a pointer can do on
    it has an HTML path beside it. Read-only: relations are edited in the post
    editor's related-posts picker. %>
<% content_for :title, t(".title") %>
<%# THE SCREEN FILLS THE WINDOW (the round of 2026-10-08): from 1,100px of
    width the heading and the box together are exactly as tall as the window
    less <main>'s padding and the top bar where there is one
    (`--admin-top-offset`), so the page does not scroll and the canvas and the
    list each take what is left. Below that width the list stands under the
    canvas, the box is as tall as its content and the page scrolls. %>
<div class="<%= "flex min-h-[560px] flex-col min-[1100px]:h-[calc(100vh_-_3rem_-_var(--admin-top-offset))]" if @content_types.any? %>">
<div class="mb-4">
  <h1 class="text-h1 text-ink"><%= t(".title") %></h1>
  <p class="mt-1 text-meta"><%= t(".intro") %></p>
</div>

<% if @content_types.empty? %>
  <%# For THIS viewer: a viewer who can read no post sees this, whatever the site holds. %>
  <div class="rounded-cs border border-line bg-surface p-6 text-meta" data-mind-graph-empty="no-posts"><%= t(".no_posts") %></div>
<% else %>
  <%# One box, three parts: the SEARCH, the GRAPH (a local view's focus bar,
      the legend and filter row, the canvas) and the LIST. In the document
      they come in that order, because the Tab key follows the document (spec
      §5.7: search, focus bar, filter, zoom buttons, canvas, card, list -- the
      list last, since it can hold two thousand rows). On screen, from
      1,100px, the graph is the left column over the box's whole height and
      the search and the list are a 300px column on its right, the search on
      top: a grid places each part, so the order of the document is free.
      Below that width they stack with the graph FIRST (`order-first`), the
      search and the list under it. The filter is three radios (arrow keys
      move between them), applied client-side.

      `data-state="loading"` is what the server says; the script takes it from
      there (`mind_graph/app.js` lists the attributes it writes). The notice is
      over the canvas's top-left corner and lets the pointer through, except
      for a button in it (Retry). The three URL templates are for the
      selection card's links: built here, by the route helpers, with `__ID__`
      and `__NAME__` where the script puts a node's id or a tag's name
      (URL-encoded), so no path is written in JavaScript; `data-type-labels`
      is each shown type's human name. `data-button-classes` and
      `data-dot-classes` hand the script the classes of
      `Admin::Ui::ButtonComponent` (the card's actions) and of
      `Admin::Ui::ContentTypeDotComponent` (a type's dot in the card and the list,
      slots 1-12 in order), so neither is copied into JavaScript.
      `data-post-notes-url` is a fourth template: a post's open notes as JSON
      for its card, and where the card posts a new one (notes spec §4.4). The
      route takes digits only (`container_id: /\d+/`), so the helper refuses
      `__ID__` (`ActionController::UrlGenerationError`): the path is built for
      id 0 and that one segment swapped. The message
      keys are written out one by one: `test/lib/script_messages_test.rb`
      reads the literals to check that every key the script asks for is
      served. %>
  <div data-controller="admin--mind-graph"
       data-url="<%= data_admin_mind_graph_path(**admin_url_options, post: params[:post].presence, tag: params[:tag].presence, depth: (@depth if @focus)) %>"
       data-worker-url="<%= asset_path("mind_graph/layout_worker.js") %>"
       data-d3-url="<%= asset_path("d3-force.js") %>"
       data-messages="<%= messages_data("mind_graph.script.loading", "mind_graph.script.load_failed", "mind_graph.script.retry", "mind_graph.script.worker_failed",
                                     "mind_graph.script.no_connections", "mind_graph.script.capped", "mind_graph.script.capped_local", "mind_graph.script.isolated", "mind_graph.script.isolated_only",
                                     "mind_graph.script.summary", "mind_graph.script.release_pinned",
                                     "mind_graph.script.card.related", "mind_graph.script.card.tags", "mind_graph.script.card.tag_posts", "mind_graph.script.card.open_post", "mind_graph.script.card.focus",
                                     "mind_graph.script.card.show_tagged", "mind_graph.script.card.close", "mind_graph.script.card.tag", "mind_graph.script.card.pin", "mind_graph.script.card.unpin",
                                     "mind_graph.script.card.status.draft", "mind_graph.script.card.status.scheduled", "mind_graph.script.card.status.live",
                                     "mind_graph.script.card.notes.title", "mind_graph.script.card.notes.label", "mind_graph.script.card.notes.add", "mind_graph.script.card.notes.sending", "mind_graph.script.card.notes.replies",
                                     "mind_graph.script.card.notes.more", "mind_graph.script.card.notes.deleted_user", "mind_graph.script.card.notes.unread", "mind_graph.script.card.notes.failed",
                                     "mind_graph.script.search.none", "mind_graph.script.search.count", "mind_graph.script.search.failed", "mind_graph.script.search.post", "mind_graph.script.search.tag",
                                     "mind_graph.script.list.posts", "mind_graph.script.list.tags", "mind_graph.script.list.empty", "mind_graph.script.list.select_post", "mind_graph.script.list.select_tag") %>"
       data-post-focus-url="<%= admin_mind_graph_path(**admin_url_options, post: "__ID__") %>"
       data-tag-focus-url="<%= admin_mind_graph_path(**admin_url_options, tag: "__ID__") %>"
       data-tag-posts-url="<%= admin_posts_path(**admin_url_options, tag: "__NAME__") %>"
       data-post-notes-url="<%= admin_record_note_threads_data_path("post", 0, **admin_url_options).sub("/0/", "/__ID__/") %>"
       data-type-labels="<%= @type_labels.to_json %>"
       data-button-classes="<%= { primary: "#{Admin::Ui::ButtonComponent::SMALL_CLASS} #{Admin::Ui::ButtonComponent::VARIANT_CLASSES[:primary]}", secondary: "#{Admin::Ui::ButtonComponent::SMALL_CLASS} #{Admin::Ui::ButtonComponent::VARIANT_CLASSES[:secondary]}" }.to_json %>"
       data-dot-classes="<%= (Admin::Ui::ContentTypeDotComponent::FILLED + Admin::Ui::ContentTypeDotComponent::RINGS).to_json %>"
       data-state="loading"
       class="grid min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-hidden rounded-cs border border-line bg-surface min-[1100px]:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_300px] min-[1100px]:grid-rows-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)]">
    <%# The search field: how a post or tag the graph doesn't draw is reached.
        Its rows are links to that row's local view, filled in by
        `mind_graph/search_box.js` with text and `href` only. The results are
        ordinary links after the field in the document, so Tab reaches them.
        The status line is the live region the results' wording goes through
        (a count, "No post or tag matches.", the failure): it stays in the DOM,
        so the list itself can stay a plain list of links. %>
    <div class="border-t border-line p-2.5 min-[1100px]:col-start-2 min-[1100px]:row-start-1 min-[1100px]:border-l min-[1100px]:border-t-0">
      <div class="relative" data-mind-graph-search data-url="<%= search_admin_mind_graph_path(**admin_url_options) %>">
        <%= label_tag "mind-graph-search", t(".search.label"), class: "sr-only" %>
        <%= search_field_tag :mind_graph_search, nil, id: "mind-graph-search", autocomplete: "off", placeholder: t(".search.placeholder"),
              class: "block w-full rounded-cs border border-line-strong bg-surface px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-ink focus:outline-2 focus:outline-accent" %>
        <p data-mind-graph-status role="status" class="sr-only"></p>
        <ul data-mind-graph-results hidden class="absolute left-0 right-0 top-full z-20 m-0 mt-1 max-h-72 list-none overflow-y-auto rounded-cs border border-line-strong bg-surface p-1 shadow-menu"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="order-first flex h-[70vh] min-h-[480px] min-w-0 flex-col min-[1100px]:order-none min-[1100px]:col-start-1 min-[1100px]:row-span-2 min-[1100px]:row-start-1 min-[1100px]:h-auto min-[1100px]:min-h-0">
      <% if @focus %>
        <%# The local view's bar (spec §5.4): what the graph is drawn around, both
            depths and the way back to the whole graph. The current depth is
            plain text marked `aria-current`, not a disabled link: it leads
            nowhere, so it is nothing to press. Read out of the row it would be
            a bare "1", so it carries the word "Depth" for a screen reader, as
            the other depth's link does in its name. All ordinary links, so Back works. The depth
            link of 1 carries no `depth`, as the screen's own URLs do. %>
        <p data-mind-graph-focus class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-1 border-b border-line px-3.5 py-2 text-sm text-dim">
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink"><%= t(".focus.around_#{@focus.kind}", title: @focus.title) %></span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5"><%= t(".focus.depth") %>
            <% [ 1, 2 ].each do |depth| %>
              <% if depth == @depth %>
                <span aria-current="true" class="font-semibold text-ink"><span class="sr-only"><%= t(".focus.depth") %></span> <%= depth %></span>
              <% else %>
                <%= link_to depth, admin_mind_graph_path(**admin_url_options, @focus.kind => @focus.id, depth: (depth if depth == 2)), "aria-label": t(".focus.depth_n", depth: depth), class: "text-accent underline" %>
              <% end %>
            <% end %>
          </span>
          <%= link_to t(".focus.whole"), admin_mind_graph_path(**admin_url_options), class: "text-accent underline" %>
        </p>
      <% end %>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-2 border-b border-line px-3.5 py-2.5">
        <%= render Admin::MindGraphLegendComponent.new(content_types: @content_types) %>
        <fieldset class="m-0 min-w-0 border-0 p-0">
          <legend class="sr-only"><%= t(".filter.legend") %></legend>
          <div class="inline-flex overflow-hidden rounded-cs border border-line-strong bg-surface">
            <% %w[all related tag].each do |value| %>
              <label for="mind-graph-filter-<%= value %>" class="flex cursor-pointer items-center border-r border-line px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-dim last:border-r-0 hover:bg-sunken has-[:checked]:bg-accent-tint has-[:checked]:font-semibold has-[:checked]:text-ink has-[:focus-visible]:outline has-[:focus-visible]:outline-2 has-[:focus-visible]:-outline-offset-2 has-[:focus-visible]:outline-accent">
                <%= radio_button_tag "mind_graph_filter", value, value == "all", id: "mind-graph-filter-#{value}", class: "sr-only", data: { action: "change->admin--mind-graph#filter" } %>
                <span><%= t(".filter.#{value}") %></span>
              </label>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
      </div>
      <%# In the document the zoom buttons come BEFORE the canvas, because the
          Tab key follows the document (spec §5.7: filter, zoom buttons, canvas);
          on screen they sit in the canvas's bottom-right corner, positioned, so
          they are painted over it whatever the order. "Release N pinned" is
          beside them only while a node is pinned: the script writes its label
          (a plural) and shows it, and the controller's `reset` hides it again.
          The zoom's figure between the two buttons is the script's too. Each
          zoom button is a glyph or a short word with its whole name as
          `aria-label` and `title`. The notice is a polite live region:
          loading, a failure and the cap's sentences are announced. %>
      <div class="relative min-h-0 flex-1">
        <div class="absolute bottom-3 right-3 flex items-stretch gap-2">
          <%= render Admin::Ui::ButtonComponent.new(label: "", variant: :secondary, size: :small, hidden: true, data: { mind_graph_release: true, action: "admin--mind-graph#releasePinned" }) %>
          <div role="group" aria-label="<%= t(".zoom") %>" class="inline-flex items-stretch overflow-hidden rounded-cs border border-line-strong bg-surface text-sm text-ink">
            <% zoom_button = "cursor-pointer px-2.5 py-0.5 font-semibold hover:bg-sunken focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:-outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent" %>
            <%= tag.button "−", type: "button", class: zoom_button, title: t(".zoom_out"), "aria-label": t(".zoom_out"), data: { action: "admin--mind-graph#zoomOut" } %>
            <span data-mind-graph-zoom class="flex min-w-12 items-center justify-center border-x border-line px-1 font-cs-mono text-label text-meta"></span>
            <%= tag.button "+", type: "button", class: zoom_button, title: t(".zoom_in"), "aria-label": t(".zoom_in"), data: { action: "admin--mind-graph#zoomIn" } %>
            <%= tag.button t(".fit_short"), type: "button", class: "#{zoom_button} border-l border-line", title: t(".fit"), "aria-label": t(".fit"), data: { action: "admin--mind-graph#fit" } %>
          </div>
        </div>
        <canvas data-admin--mind-graph-target="canvas" class="block h-full w-full touch-none text-ink focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:-outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent" role="img" tabindex="0" aria-label="<%= t(".canvas_label") %>" data-label="<%= t(".canvas_label") %>"></canvas>
        <div data-admin--mind-graph-target="notice" role="status" class="pointer-events-none absolute left-3.5 top-3 m-0 flex max-w-md flex-col gap-1 text-meta"></div>
        <%# (The canvas's `data-label` is its name as the server wrote it: the
            script puts the counts into `aria-label`, and the controller's
            `reset` puts this back on a page Turbo restored.) %>
        <%# The selection card and the hover tooltip (spec §5.3): HTML over the
            canvas, filled by `mind_graph/card.js` and `app.js` with `textContent`
            and `href` only. Both are empty and `hidden` until the script shows
            them, and the controller's `reset` hides them again on a page Turbo
            restored from its cache. The card stands beside its node: the
            script writes its `left` and `top` (`mind_graph/card_placement.js`).
            It can take the focus (`tabindex="-1"`), which a row of the list
            hands it, and is named by its title once it has one. The card's
            links are the only way a selection leads anywhere: a click on the
            canvas never navigates. %>
        <aside data-mind-graph-card hidden tabindex="-1" aria-label="<%= t(".card_label") %>" class="absolute left-0 top-0 z-10 flex w-60 max-w-[calc(100%-1rem)] flex-col gap-2 rounded-cs border border-line-strong bg-surface p-3 shadow-menu focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-accent"></aside>
        <div data-mind-graph-tooltip hidden role="presentation" class="pointer-events-none absolute z-10 max-w-xs break-words rounded-cs border border-line bg-surface px-2 py-1 text-sm text-ink shadow-menu"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <%# The list (mind graph canvas spec §5.7): every node the graph draws, as
        a row, filled by `mind_graph/node_list.js` from the same data and
        following the filter. A canvas's nodes can't take focus, so this is
        the keyboard and screen-reader path to them: a row is a button that
        selects its node, and the card it opens holds the links. It comes last
        in the document and scrolls on its own beside the canvas. Under the
        canvas it keeps a least height, so the search's results (which hang
        over it, inside the box) are not cut off by a list of two rows. %>
    <div data-mind-graph-list aria-label="<%= t(".list_label") %>" role="region" class="min-h-80 border-t border-line pb-3 min-[1100px]:col-start-2 min-[1100px]:row-start-2 min-[1100px]:min-h-0 min-[1100px]:overflow-y-auto min-[1100px]:border-l"></div>
  </div>
<% end %>
</div>
